## Decisions kept open

1. S01-11/12 sum to 576 frames / 24 seconds (240 + 336). The source showcase heading says 22 seconds. This pack keeps the machine timeline unchanged.
2. Showcase microbeats run only through relative frame 168 (169 inclusive frames / about 7.04 seconds); they do not cover 576 frames. No stretching or new exposure allocation is approved here.
3. Both shot headers specify characters on 2s; the showcase says characters on 3s and FX on 2s. Replacement drawing rates require author/director resolution.
4. S01 dialogue says fourteen became eleven. Explicit current canoe staging names eight people (four lead, one second, three third). The empty-seat description also mentions two lost, an old man and his wife against a loss of three. Preserve spoken count and staged cast; do not invent missing passengers or change the count.
5. S01-09 does not identify the owner of the snapped paddle; S01-12 still needs paddling/drag. Approve paddle ownership and subsequent hand/prop continuity before exposures.
6. S01-15 sound matches to S03 while S02 is a twelve-second intervening title. Decide the precise keyboard bridge placement without moving shots.
7. Full-episode source leaves some VO paraphrased (“as in the book, trimmed”), some dialogue/UI speaker attribution implicit, and some spoken fragments inside action. Do not fabricate complete recording copy.
8. Historical source 4:3 is superseded by current 16:9 / 24 fps. Earlier river-pack canoe assignments and dated 1523 tags are superseded by current BEFORE staging with no named year.
9. Episode source itself flags Don Chino barbershop/bodega and Fela family/name links. Yari’s relationship and window-man identity remain unrevealed in this episode. Older full-novel bible spoilers are not permission to reveal them.
10. ED has 2,160 planned frames / 90 seconds; the prose adds ten seconds of black after credits without stating whether it falls inside that budget. Body remains exactly 27,120 frames.
